Third-party components
----------------------
DSH Hub builds on third-party open-source software, each under its own license. None of it is
vendored in this repository; it is either resolved as npm dependencies (see the `package.json`
files and `pnpm-lock.yaml`) or installed into the runtime image at build time.
Notable ones:

* DeepSeek Harness (`@deepseek-ai/dsh`) — the agent runtime that runs inside each user container,
  installed from npm at runtime-image build time. Its own license applies; see the package metadata.
* sherpa-onnx (Apache-2.0) — speech recognition engine used by `services/asr`.
* SenseVoice model weights — **not distributed here**; download them yourself from their upstream
  release and check their license and terms of use before deploying.
* Vue, Naive UI, UnoCSS, Fastify, Vite, Vitest, ESLint and the rest of the npm dependency tree —
  see each package's license.

Binary artifacts (desktop installers, Android APKs) built from this repository may bundle the
runtime image and third-party icons; keep their notices with the artifact when you redistribute it.
